i02-alignment-set patch 10-ffb-discarded-draw (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (i) the random-number stream, the FFB classifier's discarded draw (E7i): the one rand()
value SAGE26 consumes and discards for each row its feedback-free-burst classifier classifies.
Campaign decisions D1, D32, D46, D47. A measurement instrument, not a proposal for Mimic.

SAGE26 behaviour: determine_and_store_ffb_regime (R/src/model_regimes.c:188-240) calls (void)rand();
(R/src/model_regimes.c:224) and discards the value, once for each row of the FoF workspace it does
not skip; it skips only rows with mergeType > 0 (:212-213), so it draws once per row with
mergeType == 0, orphans included, before that row's keyed draw halo_uniform (:225). evolve_galaxies
calls the classifier once per FoF evolution, and only when EnhancedStarFormationOn >= 1
(R/src/core_build_model.c:425-426), after the CGM classifier (:410-411, CGMrecipeOn == 1) and
infall_recipe (:415), before the substeps. At R6 (EnhancedStarFormationOn 1) the call executes.

Mimic site it changes, at the launch base 66a3e9498561e7f2f2207267a94986e9b097b03c:
models/sage26/modules/sage26_determine_ffb_regime/sage26_determine_ffb_regime.c, classify_row (:151),
whose "// SAGE parity (R/src/model_regimes.c:222-224)" comment (:152-155) marks the point of SAGE26's
discarded draw, before the row's keyed draw (:157-159). classify_row is called once for each row
sage26_determine_ffb_regime_process does not skip (:227-245; the skip, no galaxy or Type == 3, at
:231; the call at :240), and the process function writes nothing at EnhancedStarFormationOn 0
(:220-222). The file includes no <stdlib.h> (:35-37) and calls no rand().

What the patch changes: one discarded call, (void)rand();, as the first statement after that
comment in classify_row, so it executes exactly once for each row the classifier classifies at
EnhancedStarFormationOn 1, before that row's keyed draw; and #include <stdlib.h> in that file, which
the build needs (without it the file fails with "call to undeclared function 'rand'"). Nothing
else: the comment stays, and the classifier's skips, keyed draw, comparison and writes are
unchanged.

Why Mimic differs: the package calls no rand(). Its classifiers draw from keys of the halo's own
data (here SAGE26's own SplitMix64 halo_uniform, D32), not from a process-global stream consumed in
traversal order (D1, D47), as Mimic's VISION Principle 4 requires of stochastic modules, so a
galaxy's draw does not depend on the driver or the traversal. SAGE26 keeps a discarded rand() here
only so that its other draws keep their places in the libc stream; the package has no such stream
to keep in step.

Predecessor: the launch base 66a3e9498561e7f2f2207267a94986e9b097b03c with 01-particle-mass,
02-cosmic-time, 03-written-dt, 04-substep-count, 05-float-halo-state, 06-inheritance-resets,
07-written-halo-values-stacked, 08-cgm-useful-draw and 09-creation-draws applied in order. None of
them touches this file, so the patch also applies to the launch base alone.

Null control: the call only advances libc's stream. With no stream consumer (the package's keyed
CGM draw in place, no 08), it must change no galaxy.

